  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and the tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:32`, `Cart.remove` compared the SKU it was given against each item's **name** (`l.item.name != sku`). `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so nothing was ever removed. The `add` method matches on `item.sku`, so I changed `remove` to do the same:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]\n```\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- `pytest` isn't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest discover` instead: all 6 tests passed.\n\nNone of the existing tests cover `Cart.remove`, which is why this bug got through. I can add a regression test if you'd like.",
